# Tk, for APExp.  See tcl.pc beside this file for why Cflags and Libs
# are empty; the reasoning is identical.
#
# `Requires: tcl' is real rather than decorative: tk.h's own
# `#pragma lib' block names libtk BEFORE it includes <tcl.h>, because
# a kencc static link resolves archives in the order recorded and
# libtk needs libtcl.  So the dependency exists either way and saying
# it here keeps `pkg-config --exists tk' honest about what it implies.
#
# Tk also needs libdraw, libpng and libz -- its Plan 9 backend draws
# through libdraw and its photo reader uses libpng -- and all three
# are likewise named by tk.h's pragma block, which is why there is
# still nothing to put in Libs.

Name: Tk
Description: Tk toolkit (APExp, Plan 9 backend)
Version: 9.0.3
Requires: tcl
Cflags:
Libs:
